.TH geectl-pull-request-cleanup 1  "geectl-pull-request-cleanup 0.3.0" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-pull\-request\-cleanup \- Clean the local build roots for the submit request or pull request filed from the working copy in the current directory, when that request is accepted (OBS) or merged (Gitea). The reference was recorded by `submit` in the checkout; the leaf reads the state once and wipes the roots only on `accepted`/`merged`. A request in any other state, and a checkout with nothing recorded, delete nothing. A dry run still needs the recorded arm\*(Aqs credentials to build its client — dry\-run only skips the mutation, never the credential requirement. Dry\-run by default; mutates only with `\-\-live`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl pull\-request cleanup\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Clean the local build roots for the submit request or pull request filed from the working copy in the current directory, when that request is accepted (OBS) or merged (Gitea). The reference was recorded by `submit` in the checkout; the leaf reads the state once and wipes the roots only on `accepted`/`merged`. A request in any other state, and a checkout with nothing recorded, delete nothing. A dry run still needs the recorded arm\*(Aqs credentials to build its client — dry\-run only skips the mutation, never the credential requirement. Dry\-run by default; mutates only with `\-\-live`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
